    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="926da00f-14aa-554b-a93a-c5e6c6fba8c2" activityNameId="a2b6a893-599a-562b-a4e0-f8e7e2cb9337" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Modem, for customer premise equipment (CPE)</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Modem, for customer premise equipment (CPE)
The data set represents the modem networks in Switzerland; UUID: 2a7d18dd-d003-376d-be3c-64ee2ac2e8d7
The dataset is based on average of Scientific Atlanta EPC2203 &amp; Thomson TWG870 equipment. Thomson TWG870 and Scientific Atlanta EPC2203 constituted the largest proportion of the category modems (source: p. 38, SFOE 2015). Power supply unit is assumed to be 1.5019 kg/p (UVEK), router to be 0.58 kg/pcs (UVEK), and cable to be 1.04 kg/m (UVEK). Wiring is assumed to be made of copper, based on existing chasis and router datasets. Type of polymers used are taken from those found in existing chassis and router datasets. The proportion 1:1:1 is defined for HDPE:PVC:PP. No information from main literature or dataset regarding specific types of steel is available, and hence it is assumed to be low-alloyed. The total mass = 0.665 kg. The functional unit = 1 GB.
Location: Data for Swiss networks
Technology: Swiss use CPE transmission networks.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: Average technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2a7d18dd-d003-376d-be3c-64ee2ac2e8d7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
